[{"id":"VRCE-6-53-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":1,"english":"Thus addressed, Kumbhakarņa rebuking Mahodara, said to that foremost of Rākşasa-his brother-Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c8b6126fd380ea0e20574f668804a442e00df78ef8bc24247ac9f2fc247064b","compact":"f85f4250e8980f495fb496d3cc41f76fc7db4b9e78d2ceb471c5af7dfb633c76","nasal":"6d0ecc8b12aef2ee1461e7f0fa23dd74f084d4c801669785577dabe79bd7ebf6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":2,"english":"Even I shall remove your great fear by slaying the wicked minded Råma. On your foe having been slain, attain you ease.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d59578ab1a88e515f69696c40ebba316a3dd92e416e384186d11d6e7cde0c1a0","compact":"319a2ebce2a109a4cacf0fa7b317b8c953bb7eb67768bacea5367e9132a6dbf4","nasal":"319a2ebce2a109a4cacf0fa7b317b8c953bb7eb67768bacea5367e9132a6dbf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":3,"english":"It is not for naught that the heroes roar, like to clouds containing no rain. Behold you their, like roaring resulting in action in the field!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2db68e36524aeaf1ed90b4804ca50c095b911e60f5135698ec01d9b9c9bcac70","compact":"66e30297bdb07b2249b3105328e0d39cbf0e41ce5673e09798e095fbf71979f4","nasal":"aa678734414f9937e29164cbc05b39fe23331bbbe2d83b21dbfa960e822bd91c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":4,"english":"Heroes do not vaunt: but without boasting of their prowess in speech, they perform feats difficult of being achieved.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae28cc1b7dc685ed35c365d4a30fd135cd58aaf635ba3ed4ca987caade6fe2b0","compact":"be2d780d243d8ab866d7818565ae6daf7ebe66a847c733b06e96d7509a7b003c","nasal":"74f7f06e94bc25d4961813f2498a133c2be69d1853de5426eac1010e5ad89256"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":5,"english":"O Mahodara, what you say is ever acceptable only to kings that are incompetent, and foolish, pluming themselves on their knowledge.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.385,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f1b6ab4b67aed02ffe449f02f8a752f5f8ee6bd85680142f7429c3a9c981401","compact":"2c6a97a890546b8b890a109588870b954c7913801014d34f80beb1f0ee4cc6c0","nasal":"a55a2af60806690d55490cc2bb9c9959dfc72c8d92b33ba63d7a16e842864684"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":6,"english":"All the affairs of the monarch have been wrecked by you-cravens in fight, sleek-tongued, following the king (fawning) you have made Lankā contain only the king, the treasury is lean; and the forces have been slain. By the king you have done like foes in the guise of friends.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19117c16e40bbade6665503671d86799ef508450872a8599e8537586306594d5","compact":"4ba15090c550c1d21abe9107202bbb8e8bded3e405ba24b29bc727e305cc3136","nasal":"4ba15090c550c1d21abe9107202bbb8e8bded3e405ba24b29bc727e305cc3136"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":7,"english":"All the affairs of the monarch have been wrecked by you-cravens in fight, sleek-tongued, following the king (fawning) you have made Lankā contain only the king, the treasury is lean; and the forces have been slain. By the king you have done like foes in the guise of friends.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac317b45148a4dfd9304e9c5baa850278d4c9d9d2094bc9e852b66c6a20c41ff","compact":"77a104b126ab88c8a676e85b4a22945b42a92e5e54bd67cfc5c143ccc7adb93f","nasal":"19bbc30b55b80e98fa9ae22bb019f625f954564662aed7811d0e786ecf0ba7b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":8,"english":"For repairing in mighty conflict the wrong that you have perpetrated, I am about to set out for battle for routing the enemy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16b889cc336051c021984b0012b2a7cbf32ac7164b341479aa03b5cc4f7f562e","compact":"bfad5d30cddb6a223a072e48c99ae7ee529781dbd2f9b3df6ceb9a191ff94ddc","nasal":"bfad5d30cddb6a223a072e48c99ae7ee529781dbd2f9b3df6ceb9a191ff94ddc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":9,"english":"Thus addressed by the intelligent Kumbhakarna, the lord of Raksasas, laughing answered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da85f4539a99b67a1a4c213340821b5312094d124cd5ab369febf5ac1ca339bd","compact":"2bcb1c2580746409120f083a750490f122a07f3182d3e2055001aea0dc2aa6d2","nasal":"bf2ca63b8851fd8d7131a89a243b7110271953d827437c1c006c10dcc0a3c878"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":10,"english":"Sure this Mahodara is affrighted at Rāma. Therefore, my child, O you versed in warfare, he does not relish battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"038c9a15b5ae158f81507723e87b658a2e84f5e760b70d8b1dd7c4c31fd81c8c","compact":"9f73d4e3ad96c00a769bde4832674ac3963436de16f0e65a79174d9e27f10636","nasal":"9f73d4e3ad96c00a769bde4832674ac3963436de16f0e65a79174d9e27f10636"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":11,"english":"Like you have I none either in friendship or strength. Therefore, O Kumbhakama, go for destroying the foe and securing celebrity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2494d535df635c72757f7a67f69da8a1cd137e55ad47c88961cdd467eaf1b36f","compact":"4113a36157d434323db72facec03f19a35c96be949221f9c1ec15549568698be","nasal":"679b9181714a90a6daa14253d864fe3d6b484e110d2e8421590933276d54b5d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":12,"english":"He took a whetted dart, destructive to foes on account of its impetuous vehemence; entirely made of black iron; flaming: decorated with garniture, of shining gold; looking like Indra's asani; ponderous as the thunder-bolt; capable of destroying gods and Dānavas, Gandharvas, Yakşas and Pannagas, adorned with festoons of crimson flowers; and belching forth flames. And taking that huge dart decked with the blood of foes. The wondrous energetic Kumbhakarna spoke to Ravana, saying, I shall go alone; let this mighty host remain here.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9cc4bf78dd6092252e9d5cc0b0caec8fa3b592ddc03aab0174dc98ad15ce1e4f","compact":"4df476dfbc2e8fd116b3d6cb42f68a277917cdbd3b8308776c590fc445c75efd","nasal":"44723c03b2d45f157c14fd979b7a3dd62df2abbb7ef5c0e0a377a98228620eb3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":13,"english":"He took a whetted dart, destructive to foes on account of its impetuous vehemence; entirely made of black iron; flaming: decorated with garniture, of shining gold; looking like Indra's asani; ponderous as the thunder-bolt; capable of destroying gods and Dānavas, Gandharvas, Yakşas and Pannagas, adorned with festoons of crimson flowers; and belching forth flames. And taking that huge dart decked with the blood of foes. The wondrous energetic Kumbhakarna spoke to Ravana, saying, I shall go alone; let this mighty host remain here.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.6,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d84367427fae8df7587428cbf1ea770f110f847b08439e71cec3f3ba74872f41","compact":"f7b47208d11ccb7f2222dfebcc6ba1235a60a56218fd3f3dfbe