ted themselves on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f6e34e5d6292f922cfb4e23d41d21a778837e8d826b9ab463ba71caa2689dcc9","compact":"eafd80ec9a1492ebacba474d8a222269f45e72bb0ba835664a0e6f0dbea19613","nasal":"de9a383196f6d03b65eaff71271692484a1ca3cfda0f5fb94fe5450ad6397856"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":41,"english":"Clouds containing meteors and lightning looked dark like asses. And the earth shook with her oceans and woods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.62,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2484de17170b2cde7cd50cf764ae649f807ecc007bf7d76fc081843298b34b4","compact":"4eb04fa6f8f23885f22f5be68c27b4eee92b4f59172db830f0ec1901198410c0","nasal":"1a07f5f56cba65e351cdfe68ea11d0e5dc87afc609d090ad9c78c287ca714710"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":42,"english":"And fierce jackals began to cry, opening their fiaming mouths. And birds began to wheel at the left.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f7ad4a9eb7367390daaeb98a3ef7fa7fec4c812b67ddab262edb627e71d328e","compact":"eb7bb5ab6ea6b0482560210448cc1a611264d2982ab82be01592048932f3d989","nasal":"a50291bc4a51d209d1a195a59b9ec48f00248e371f239b416c095e709e11582f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":43,"english":"As he marched a vulture alighted on his dart. And his left eye throbbed and his left arm shook.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1cea107e691f61e0ebdd28ab2290e0246c210c941fa28d23884ae6171396a94","compact":"82888b79b36924811183783517c4185a358c2346f1bec3c233fcfd43661ed0c8","nasal":"9c9b4aafdaa736957e63fc1a85f30277f583c66b62c5f17915aaf468aaaec210"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":44,"english":"A meteor dropped down with a tremendous crash. And the sun was bedimmed, and the air did not blow, enhancing pleasure.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fcb5ef45a41380d550ae6100873c9b97ffc74101cdf16cc87f4b8a74a45fcc8f","compact":"3cde369d30084d5044ae08ecf9df57e8ea1add533a671d8fba1ac93cd3d43455","nasal":"45f5ce53132b285ac20cd8ade00b6df31591ba1e9d0b9fb078924afbe064e9de"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":53,"verse":45,"english":"But without heeding these mighty omens that took place, capable of making people's down stand on end, Kumbhakarna went out, urged on by the force of the Finisher.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-65-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6053045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"435f2063c8a3f908dc7866bb2e2b7585b32b91d26e5a2e38a3bddb4c7c7c980c","compact":"7fb11aaaff440062077234e2fe948f730f85c713b5bc111e04d43dcde4892f8d","nasal":"411886fd896a6a8bb698a698624fa1178b765b821027352b63d6594dd0875360"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-53-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"y